# The fusions of one part that eliminate nothing, beside the part they carry. One row per such
# fusion per quantity, with the part's figure and the composed figure side by side.
#
# Carrying needs no arithmetic
#   A fusion of one part that eliminates nothing is the one case where composing needs no
#   arithmetic at all, which makes it the sharpest test here. It must reproduce that part: there is
#   nothing to add, nothing to subtract, and no judgement to make. So any difference is a defect
#   with no defence, and it can be asked of every quantity rather than only the ones the sum rule
#   composes.
#
# Five quantities: demand, nameplate and the three slacks
#   `checks/fusion_sum_disagrees` reads composition/fused.sqlc, which adds up demand, nameplate and
#   draw; `checks/window_lost_or_summed` covers the calendar. Nothing adds up the three buffer
#   slacks, so this relation is where a one-part fusion is held to them.
#
# A suspension removes only the quantity it names
#   A fusion suspended for its draw alone still carries its demand and nameplate, so the anti-join
#   matches on the quantity, or on a NULL quantity, which suspends them all.
#
# A one-part fusion is not degenerate
#   `every-local-part` says so in its own words: a one-part fusion says this reviewer read that
#   layer and carried it. Carrying is an assertion, so it is something that can be got wrong.
#
# The factor still applies
#   A single part may be converted into the composed layer's unit, so carried unchanged means "the
#   part, converted" rather than "the part, copied".
#
# A factor filed as absent is left out, not read as one
#   Filling a missing factor with one is right only where the blank means there is no conversion to
#   make. `asrt:factor` is a `pm:StatedFactor`, so its absent branch carries a typed reason, and
#   `every-unsized-conversion/shift-capacity` files `unmeasured` on one of its parts: a composer
#   saying nobody measured the conversion. Read as one, that becomes "the units are the same", a
#   claim they declined to make. Carrying cannot be asserted across a conversion nobody sized, so
#   those parts leave this relation.
#
# An omitted factor is a different state, and it stays
#   `minOccurs="0"` and no factor means no conversion is needed, which is the sender asserting the
#   units already agree. That is a filing; `unmeasured` is a gap.
#
# Two quantity types meet here
#   A suspension names its quantity as `pm.summed_quantity`, the three a fusion adds up; a candidate
#   carries `public.layer_quantity`, the five a layer states. Both are declared types, and they
#   agree on `demand` and `nameplate` and on nothing else. So both sides cast to text, because the
#   name is all the two types share. Drop either cast and Postgres refuses the comparison, which is
#   the right refusal: nothing quietly converts one type into the other.
#
# The difference against a named candidate set
#   The candidate set is a file, composition/carriable.sqlc, and this is the difference taken
#   against it. Both operands are named, so algebra/carried.sqlc can count them. Fold the two
#   `NOT EXISTS` back into a `WHERE` over an inline candidate set and the law loses its left
#   operand: the SQL still runs, the rows are identical, and nothing on algebra/roster.sqlc can be
#   written about it.
-- composition/carriable.sqlc less the fusions that eliminate or owe no sum.
SELECT c.*
FROM      (
    :compose(composition/carriable.sqlc)
) c
WHERE NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1 FROM ( :compose(eliminations/filed.sqlc) ) e
        WHERE e.composition = c.filing AND e.composed_layer = c.layer)
  AND NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1 FROM ( :compose(composition/suspended_quantities.sqlc) ) s
        WHERE s.composition = c.filing AND s.composed_layer = c.layer
          AND s.quantity::text = c.quantity::text)
